//
// These annotations carry only SQS concepts: standard and FIFO queues and
// their attributes, dead-letter queues, access policies, sending and
// receiving, and the region and account of the queues. Everything generic
// (info, servers, security schemes, tags, summaries, examples, headers, ...)
// uses the asyncapi.v3 annotations (asyncapi/v3/annotations.proto). Message
// attributes are documented as message headers.
//
// The generated documents use the official AsyncAPI SQS bindings (0.2.0);
// what they do not define is added as x-sqs extensions.
//
// A service only needs enough annotations to say "this is an SQS API";
// everything else is inferred from the Protobuf schema and its comments:
//
//   - send vs. receive vs. request/reply is inferred from the rpc shape, as
//     documented on Pattern;
//   - queue names default to "<package>-<service>-<method>", with the
//     package's dots as dashes and names in snake_case;
